  "ownership": "Hand-authored product adaptation on the canonical Core editor/Form state; pinned ARB value extraction verified against all existing selection labels. No feature-specific converter was added.",
  "scope": "Selected Stateful Cupertino field, rounded/default/disabled/borderless decoration, placeholder baseline stack, text-driven prefix/suffix/clear precedence, shared style/lines/input/focus/controller/completion and FormRow validation/save/reset. Core paragraph cursor/strut/scaler, mobile/desktop selection controls, Core adaptive toolbar and mobile magnifier configuration now use the same editor owner. Source readonly-child/ARGB/host adaptations are explicit. Full public editing/caret/strut/cursor/obscuring/selection/toolbar/magnifier/spelling/restoration and native font/IME/physical parity remain PARTIAL. Programmatic composition replacement waits for authoritative OS cancellation when available and otherwise rejects explicitly. Clear keyboard/semantic focus uses the existing Core ControlInteraction; pointer clearing preserves editor focus. Public onTapOutside/onTapUpOutside callbacks and groupId share Core policy. The complete decoration/prefix/suffix/clear region uses the declared group identity; propagating a custom group to the outer design region is an explicit Core adaptation beyond the pinned outer region default. enableInteractiveSelection defaults to !readOnly || !obscureText and is forwarded to the Core editor. Disabled pointer selection preserves the caret while requesting input focus. Public scrollController/scrollPhysics forward to the actual Core Scrollable/ScrollPosition. Borrowed controllers retain caller ownership. Design text/controller restoration remains separate from Core offset restoration."
}
